<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<CustomField xmlns="http://soap.sforce.com/2006/04/metadata">
    <!--
        DISPOSITION GAP CLOSURE TRANCHE 5 (FINAL), ITEM 2 (agent-output/disposition-gap-closure-t5-design.md
        G-3; Gate 1 decision, 2026-09-02). NO TYPE CHANGE, NO FORMULA, NO WRITER ADDED - this field
        stays a bare hand-typed Date. Only inlineHelpText was added, documenting that fact.

        🔴 A DAILY JOB TO MAINTAIN THIS FIELD WAS DESIGNED AND DELIBERATELY DEFERRED ON 2026-09-02.
        The design named DispositionTractionService.evaluateAll as the intended seam - its own header
        already states it is 2 SOQL for any number of dispositions and explicitly designs for a
        caller exactly like this one. It was not built this tranche because a Schedulable is inert
        until someone runs System.schedule post-deploy and fails silently with zero errors if nobody
        does - a risk this tranche chose not to carry alongside its other, verifiable items.

        ⚠ A FORMULA ALTERNATIVE WAS CONSIDERED AND REJECTED, NOT MERELY DEFERRED. The offers clause
        and the traction clock's pause behaviour cannot be expressed in a formula field, so a formula
        would flag listings that already have offers as still needing a check-in - a false alarm, not
        a simplification. This is why the deferred fix is a scheduled job calling the service, not a
        formula on this field.

        Until that job exists, this field is populated only by hand (or by seed scripts) and the
        Broker Alert Due dashboard KPI is only as current as the last manual edit. See inlineHelpText
        below for the user-facing version of this note.
    -->
    <fullName>Next_Broker_Checkin__c</fullName>
    <inlineHelpText>Hand-maintained only. No formula, flow, trigger, or batch job writes this field - only a person, by editing the record. The Broker Alert Due dashboard KPI filters on this date (NEXT_N_DAYS:7) and depends entirely on someone updating it after each broker check-in; if nobody does, the KPI silently goes stale rather than erroring. A daily job to maintain it was designed and deliberately deferred - see this field's XML comment.</inlineHelpText>
    <label>Next Broker Check-in</label>
    <required>false</required>
    <trackHistory>false</trackHistory>
    <trackTrending>false</trackTrending>
    <type>Date</type>
</CustomField>
